{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T10:06:21.540729", "data": {"url": "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/saurabhsinghz_remembering-jamshedji-tata-the-founding-activity-7302272296931446785-CHAe", "title": "Remembering Jamshedji Tata, the founding father of TATA group on his birth anniversary!\n\nJamsetji Nusserwanji Tata, India's first industrial pioneer, was a visionary who dreamed of a modern India\u2026 | SAURABH SINGH | 21 comments", "content": "SAURABH SINGH\u2019s Post SAURABH SINGH 1y Report this post Remembering Jamshedji Tata, the founding father of TATA group on his birth anniversary! Jamsetji Nusserwanji Tata, India's first industrial pioneer, was a visionary who dreamed of a modern India long before his time. In 1868, with Rs 21,000, he founded his first trading company, eventually transforming the landscape of Indian industry. His goals were clear: -Build an iron and steel company -Establish a world-class educational institution -Create a unique hotel, and -Harness hydroelectric power While only the Taj Hotel became a reality during his lifetime, it made history in its own right. Inaugurated on December 3, 1903, at a cost of Rs 42 million, the Taj was the first hotel in India to have electricity\u2014a revolutionary feat at the time. Though he didn't live to see all his dreams fulfilled, Jamsetji's successors carried them forward, building the iconic Tata Steel, IISc, and Tata Power. Today, his legacy continues to inspire generations. 1,267 21 Comments Like Comment Share Copy LinkedIn Facebook X Vikas Pundora 1y Report this comment SAURABH SINGH Jamshedji Tata teaches us the importance of combining visionary innovation with genuine care for people. His commitment to social welfare reminds us that business success should uplift communities and foster long-term progress. We can learn to pursue excellence while always keeping ethics, sustainability, and community development at the forefront. Like Reply 2 Reactions 3 Reactions Shraddha Bharuka 1y Report this comment Jamsetji Tata\u2019s vision shaped India\u2019s future! His legacy of innovation and progress continues to inspire generations. Like Reply 1 Reaction 2 Reactions Suchit Chaurasia 1y Report this comment Love this Like Reply 1 Reaction 2 Reactions Srishti Kashyap 1y Report this comment This legacy continues to inspire India. His vision paved the way of Modern India. \ud83d\ude4f\ud83d\ude4f Like Reply 1 Reaction 2 Reactions Aakash Verma 1y Report this comment Jamsetji Tata's vision truly paved the way for modern India, inspiring entrepreneurs like us to dream big! Like Reply 1 Reaction 2 Reactions Sitanshu Tripathi 1y Report this comment Thank you for sharing this inspiring tribute to Jamsetji Tata. His vision and pioneering spirit truly laid the foundation for modern Indian industry. It's remarkable how his principles of innovation, integrity, and social responsibility continue to guide the Tata Group today. His emphasis on community welfare and sustainable development set a benchmark for corporate citizenship long before it became a global norm. Celebrating his legacy reminds us of the power of visionary leadership and the enduring impact it can have on society. Like Reply 1 Reaction 2 Reactions Rohit Dosi 1y Report this comment He was the world's most generous donor and donated more than 8 lakh crore rupees, more than anyone in the world, including Bill Gates, Elon Musk, Mukesh Ambani, and Zuckerberg . Like Reply 1 Reaction 2 Reactions Fahmitha Fathima 1y Report this comment SAURABH SINGH Jamsetji Tata\u2019s legacy continues to inspire. His vision shaped India\u2019s industrial landscape, from Tata Steel to the Taj Hotel. A true pioneer whose dreams live on through generations. Like Reply 1 Reaction 2 Reactions Himanshu Chanda 1y Report this comment TCS still with the same vision offering 21000 as starting package. Like Reply 1 Reaction Yash Singh 1y Report this comment Thank you, SAURABH SINGH , for honoring the legacy of Jamshedji Tata so eloquently. It's remarkabl