aj Hotel became a reality during his lifetime, it made history in its own right.\n\nInaugurated on December 3, 1903, at a cost of Rs 42 million, the Taj was the first hotel in India to have electricity\u2014a revolutionary feat at the time.\n\nThough he didn't live to see all his dreams fulfilled, Jamsetji's successors carried them forward, building the iconic Tata Steel, IISc, and Tata Power.\n\nToday, his legacy continues to inspire generations. | 21 comments on LinkedIn", "meta_keywords": "", "og_image": "https://media.licdn.com/dms/image/v2/D5622AQEy0Nm1kinOuQ/feedshare-shrink_1280/B56ZVbh8vxGQAk-/0/1740997383647?e=2147483647&v=beta&t=DZrsYQg6Ns_P1oqQF3zicmmQQU9ykO-dN0ABiD3xDEo", "js_rendered": true, "js_message": "Page appears to be rendered by a JavaScript framework; content may be incomplete.", "success": true, "error": "", "truncated": false, "fetched_bytes": 191985, "total_bytes": 191985}}